# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# `target/` alone is several GB and would be copied into the builder only to be
# ignored — and worse, a host-built `target/` can shadow the container's own
# artifacts and produce an image built from stale objects.
target/
.git/
.github/

# Secrets never enter the build context, even though the Dockerfile does not
# copy them: a `.env` in an image layer is a `.env` published to Docker Hub.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Documentation, planning artifacts and the vendored specification are ~50 MB
# and none of it is compiled.
docs/
_bmad-output/
_bmad/
.claude/

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
